today we're going to show you a demo of  oxides new 3d engine nitrous this 3d  benchmark called star swarm is running  on AMD's new mantel API  AMD's mantle api is particularly well  suited for nitrous because it supports a  high degree of parallelism  what makes nitrous special is that if  it's truly core neutral every CPU core  talks to the GPU nitrous already has  three games in active development using  the engine and a demo of this will soon  be available to download from Steam so  you can see it for yourself  nitrous delivers bleeding edge  performance on DirectX as well but to  maintain the frame rate we have to back  off on some high-end graphics options  like motion blur multi samples with  motion blur disabled our performance  increases dramatically each of those  ships is prioritizing threats and  battling according to its AI every laser  blast and missile is an independent  physics object nitrous opens new doors  for game designers with these kinds of  capabilities with motion blur back on  star swarm drops significantly but it  gives you a preview of the kinds of  movie effects we will soon see in games  because nitrous has been designed from  the ground up to take advantage of the  multi-core CPUs game designers can  envision new types of games that simply  weren't possible before one of the  secrets behind nitrous is its  implementation of object space rendering  the same general technique high-end  movie CGI effects studios use except  nitrous can render it in a game in real  time we didn't want to sacrifice detail  in fidelity to chase a unit count though  nitrous can render little details as  well as big scenes check out the capital  ships turrets note that each ship has  turrets that track independently the  hyper efficient use of the CPU and the  nitrous engine frees up processing power  to be spent on other  play features for example we now have  enough cpu to simulate gravity  individual / ship turrets muzzle flashes  and more these little touches lended  intangible realism to any game imagine  them playing out on the truly massive  scale that nitrous enables nitrous opens  doors for game designers to explore new  experiences that aren't possible using  earlier technology the scope a nitrous  powered game can achieve is only the  beginning of the next generation of  strategy games and we can't wait to see  what talented game designers do with our  engine
 

